This directory contains a QuIDDPro script which simulates a randomly
generated circuit consisting of Toffoli gates.  A program to generate
other random circuits of this form is also included.

The program is called "rand_toff."  It takes two command-line
arguments.  The first argument is the number of desired qubits in the
circuit (must be greater than 2).  The second argument is the number
of desired gates in the circuit.  The generated QuIDDPro script is
simply sent to standard out.  So, to store the generated QuIDDPro
script to a file, redirect standard out to a file.  For example,

./rand_toff 200 1000 > toff200.qpro

will create a 200-qubit random circuit with 1000 gates consisting of
Toffoli gates.

Scripts
-------

toff200_1.qpro: A 100-qubit random circuit with 1000 gates consisting of
                Toffoli gates

toff200_2.qpro: A 100-qubit random circuit with 1000 gates consisting of
                Toffoli gates

toff200_3.qpro: A 100-qubit random circuit with 1000 gates consisting of
                Toffoli gates

toff200_4.qpro: A 100-qubit random circuit with 1000 gates consisting of
                Toffoli gates

toff200_5.qpro: A 100-qubit random circuit with 1000 gates consisting of
                Toffoli gates
